---
title: "Custom Tooltip Component"
---

A custom tooltip component replaces the content and styling of the grid's default tooltip. Set `tooltipComponent` on a column or column group to use it, and pass it options with `tooltipComponentParams`. The component can draw its own [arrows](#arrows) and can be [interactive](./tooltips-show-hide/#interactive-tooltips).

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    defaultColDef: {
        tooltipComponent: CustomTooltip,
    },
    columnDefs: [
        { field: 'athlete', tooltip: true, tooltipComponentParams: { color: '#55AA77' } },
    ],
};
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Tooltip with Arrow" name="custom-tooltip-component" /%}

## Tooltip Locations

`params.location` identifies where the tooltip is shown, for example `'cell'`, `'header'`, `'setFilterValue'`, `'menu'` or `'richSelectListItem'`.

Column/group `tooltipComponent` settings apply to:

- Cells, cell validation/formula errors and full-width group rows.
- Column/group headers and tool-panel labels.
- Set Filter items and row group, pivot and value panel pills.

Other sources, such as menu items, Rich Select values/items and Advanced Filter messages, use the default tooltip component. To customise these, [override `agTooltipComponent`](./components/#overriding-grid-components). Source metadata such as `column`, `node` and `data` is supplied only where applicable.

Automatic truncated-text previews use the same component selection as configured tooltips at each location.

[Built-in control tooltips](./tooltips-built-in/#custom-component) use `builtInTooltipComponent` instead and do not inherit column/group customisations.

