{% if isFramework("react") %}
{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="CustomTooltipProps" /%}
{% /if %}

`ITooltipParams<TData, TValue, TContext, TTooltipValue>` contains the resolved tooltip `value` and optional `hideTooltipCallback`. `TValue` describes column cells; the optional fourth generic describes a different tooltip payload and defaults to `TValue`. Tooltip component selectors receive arbitrary resolved content, which need not match the column's cell value type.

## Arrows

Each tooltip element receives an `ag-tooltip-position-<position>` class for its resolved placement. `--ag-tooltip-arrow-offset` gives the physical distance to the arrow centre, measured from the **left** edge for top/bottom placements or the **top** edge for left/right placements, including in RTL. Use these in custom arrow CSS; placement is not passed to the component's params. Custom components must clamp the offset to suit their own dimensions, arrow size and corner radius, as the example above does.
